# Shared configuration for the operator CLI tools in cmd/.
#
# In the trading monorepo these Makefiles pulled KAFKA_BROKERS and friends from
# ../../../../{Makefile.variables,common.env,local.env}. Those includes did not
# survive extraction, so the targets are defined here instead and the tools are
# runnable straight from this repo.
#
# Override any value on the command line, e.g.
#   make backup DATADIR=/Volumes/other WORKERS=4

# Kafka is reached over the shared cluster's EXTERNAL nodeport listener, which is
# routable from a laptop on the LAN. All three broker nodes are listed for
# bootstrap redundancy. The monorepo's local.env pointed at 192.168.178.38 -- a
# master, not a broker -- which worked only because the listener uses
# externalTrafficPolicy=Cluster. These are the actual brokers.
KAFKA_BROKERS ?= 192.168.178.41:32159,192.168.178.42:32159,192.168.178.43:32159

# Backup store. Previously only cmd/backup defined this; cmd/cleaner and
# cmd/restore referenced ${DATADIR} with nothing setting it, so they ran with
# -datadir="". Defining it here fixes both.
DATADIR ?= /Volumes/kafka-topic-backup

# kubectlquant is a zsh function (~/.zsh/k8s.zsh), so targets that enumerate
# KafkaTopics only work from an interactive zsh. Kafka still lives on the quant
# cluster; revisit if it moves.
KUBECTL_KAFKA ?= kubectlquant
